rver lookups#Retrieve server data using g\\_scratchpad":[58,89],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Minimize server lookups#Retrieve server data using g\\_scratchpad#{1}":[60,67],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Minimize server lookups#Retrieve server data using g\\_scratchpad#{2}":[68,68],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Minimize server lookups#Retrieve server data using g\\_scratchpad#{3}":[69,69],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Minimize server lookups#Retrieve server data using g\\_scratchpad#{4}":[70,71],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Minimize server lookups#Retrieve server data using g\\_scratchpad#{5}":[72,89],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Minimize server lookups#Retrieve server data using asynchronous GlideAjax":[90,151],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Minimize server lookups#Retrieve server data using asynchronous GlideAjax#{1}":[92,151],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Use the setValue\\(\\) displayValue parameter for reference fields":[152,175],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Use the setValue\\(\\) displayValue parameter for reference fields#{1}":[154,175],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Use UI policy instead of a client script":[176,186],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Use UI policy instead of a client script#{1}":[178,181],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Use UI policy instead of a client script#{2}":[182,182],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Use UI policy instead of a client script#{3}":[183,184],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Use UI policy instead of a client script#{4}":[185,186],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Validating the input by using a client script":[187,200],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Validating the input by using a client script#{1}":[189,200],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Set client script order":[201,223],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Set client script order#{1}":[203,204],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Set client script order#Before you begin":[205,208],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Set client script order#Before you begin#{1}":[207,208],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Set client script order#About this task":[209,212],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Set client script order#About this task#{1}":[211,212],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Set client script order#Procedure":[213,223],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Set client script order#Procedure#{1}":[215,216],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Set client script order#Procedure#{2}":[217,218],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Set client script order#Procedure#{3}":[219,220],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Set client script order#Procedure#{4}":[221,223],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Avoid DOM manipulation":[224,229],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Avoid DOM manipulation#{1}":[226,229],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Avoid global client scripts":[230,237],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Avoid global client scripts#{1}":[232,237],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Enclose code in functions":[238,271],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Enclose code in functions#{1}":[240,271],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Run only necessary scripts":[272,436],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Run only necessary scripts#{1}":[274,436],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Related":[437,442],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Related#{1}":[439,439],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Related#{2}":[440,440],"#Client-side scripting design and processing#Related#{3}":[441,442]},"outlinks":[{"title":"client scripts","target":"client-scripts","line":24},{"title":"Client-side scripting","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/api-reference/scripts/client-side-scripting-overview.md","line":35},{"title":"scripting","target":"c_Script","line":52},{"title":"client-side scripting","target":"client-side-scripting-overview","line":64},{"title":"Configuring the form layout","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/platform-administration/configure-form-layout.md","line":217},{"title":"Client-side scripting","target":"client-side-scripting-overview","line":439},{"title":"Client scripts","target":"client-scripts","line":440},{"title":"Scripting","target":"c_Script","line":441}],"metadata":{"title":"Client-side scripting design and processing","description":"Well-designed client scripts can reduce the amount of time it takes users to complete a form.If you create UI policies or client scripts for fields on a form, you must use another method to ensure that data in those fields is similarly controlled in a list.Use client data as much as possible to eliminate the need for time-consuming server lookups.When using setValue\\(\\) on a reference field, include the displayValue parameter to avoid additional server calls.When possible, consider using a UI policy instead of a client script.An excellent use for a client script is to validate the input from the user.Control the order of execution for your client scripts using the Order field. To avoid having two or more client scripts run concurrently and then conflict, you can add an order for the scripts to run in. Avoid Document Object Model \\(DOM\\) manipulation if possible. It can cause a maintainability issue when browsers are updated.A global client script is any client script where the selected Table is Global. Global client scripts have no table restrictions, therefore they will load on every page in the system introducing browser load delay in the process.Enclose the code in a client script inside a function.To avoid running time-consuming scripts unnecessarily, make sure that client scripts perform only necessary tasks.","locale":"en-US","canonical_url":"https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/api-reference/scripts/client-script-best-practices.html","release":"australia","product":"Scripts","classification":"scripts","topic_type":"concept","last_updated":"2026-06-25","reading_time_minutes":11,"breadcrumb":["Client-side scripting","Scripting","API implementation","API implementation and reference"],"tags":["#api-reference","#script-includes","#server-side","#glideajax","#library","#type-concept"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[[74,78],[82,88],[96,118],[122,150],[160,165],[169,174],[195,199],[246,255],[259,268],[280,289],[293,310],[316,337],[341,349],[353,375],[381,405],[409,435]],"key":"ServiceNowOfficialDocs/api-reference/scripts/client-script-best-practices.md"},
